From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:44:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 56/66] mac80211: ath11k: look for firmware-N.bin without the
 user-space fallback

ath11k patch 116 (for upstream), B123: ath11k asks for the optional
firmware-2.bin with firmware_request_nowarn(), which on OpenWrt
(CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK=y) still hands a missing file to
procd's loader. Every probe of a QCN9074 that runs from amss.bin alone
then logged the miss, and when airscan unbound the scan radio right
after probing, procd failed to write its answer ("Bad file descriptor").
Request the file with request_firmware_direct(), as ath11k already does
for its optional calibration file.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile              |  2 +-
 ....bin-without-the-user-space-fallback.patch | 44 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100755 package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/116-wifi-ath11k-look-for-firmware-N.bin-without-the-user-space-fallback.patch

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
index fc14ba4716..235f282047 100644
--- a/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/Makefile
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ PKG_NAME:=mac80211
 
 PKG_SOURCE_VERSION:=7.2
 PKG_VERSION:=$(subst -,_,$(PKG_SOURCE_VERSION))
-PKG_RELEASE:=24
+PKG_RELEASE:=25
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0-only
 PKG_LICENSE_FILES:=COPYING
 
diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/116-wifi-ath11k-look-for-firmware-N.bin-without-the-user-space-fallback.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/116-wifi-ath11k-look-for-firmware-N.bin-without-the-user-space-fallback.patch
new file mode 100755
index 0000000000..a8155ac3a9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/ath11k/116-wifi-ath11k-look-for-firmware-N.bin-without-the-user-space-fallback.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH ath-next] wifi: ath11k: look for firmware-N.bin without the
+ user-space fallback
+
+ath11k_fw_pre_init() asks for firmware-2.bin through
+ath11k_core_firmware_request(), that is firmware_request_nowarn(), and
+falls back to API 1 when the file is not there. The file is optional,
+and many installations have none: on an Arista C-360 the QCN9074 runs
+from amss.bin alone. With CONFIG_FW_LOADER_USER_HELPER_FALLBACK, which
+OpenWrt sets, firmware_request_nowarn() still hands a missing file to
+the user-space loader, so every probe of such a device waits on a
+uevent and its answer, and the loader logs the miss; when the device
+goes away before the answer, as when it is unbound right after probing,
+the loader then fails to write its answer:
+
+  procd: Failed to write to .../firmware/ath11k!QCN9074!hw1.0!firmware-2.bin/loading: Bad file descriptor
+
+Request it with request_firmware_direct() instead, which looks on the
+filesystem only, as ath11k already does for the optional calibration
+file in ath11k_qmi_load_bdf_qmi().
+
+Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
+Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
++++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/fw.c
+@@ -16,10 +16,14 @@
+ 	struct ath11k_fw_ie *hdr;
+ 	const u8 *data;
+ 	__le32 *timestamp;
++	char path[100];
+ 
+-	ab->fw.fw = ath11k_core_firmware_request(ab, name);
+-	if (IS_ERR(ab->fw.fw)) {
+-		ret = PTR_ERR(ab->fw.fw);
++	/* The file is optional: look for it on the filesystem only, so a
++	 * missing one does not go through the user-space fallback loader.
++	 */
++	ath11k_core_create_firmware_path(ab, name, path, sizeof(path));
++	ret = request_firmware_direct(&ab->fw.fw, path, ab->dev);
++	if (ret) {
+ 		ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_BOOT, "failed to load %s: %d\n", name, ret);
+ 		ab->fw.fw = NULL;
+ 		return ret;
-- 
